SUMMARY:Earth Day at Greenfield
DESCRIPTION:At Greenfield\, caring for the planet isn’t just something we talk about—it’s a responsibility we live out together. Environmental stewardship has long been a core value across Greenfield\, the High Companies\, and the High Foundation\, and our annual Earth Day Celebration is one of the ways we honor that commitment. \n\n\n\nJoin us on April 22 as we come together with fellow community members to celebrate the natural world around us. In partnership with the Lancaster Conservancy\, this year’s event invites guests to step into an enchanting world inspired by the textures and beauty of moss\, ferns\, and wild landscapes—a setting created to spark wonder\, creativity\, and connection. \n\n\n\nGuests will enjoy an engaging mix of hands‑on activities\, including: \n\n\n\nGoat Cuddling with friendly baby goatsA Painting Station featuring custom wooden mushrooms to decorate and take homeThe Faire Flower Shoppe\, where guests design whimsical pressed‑flower fairy silhouettes \n\n\n\n\n    learn more
URL:https://figlancaster.com/event/earth-day-at-greenfield/
LOCATION:Greenfield Park\, 1861 William Penn Way\, Lancaster\, Pennsylvania\, 17601\, United States
CATEGORIES:Community,Festivals & Annual Events
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/webp:https://fig.guide/content/uploads/sites/3/2026/04/photo-apr-16-2025-11-50-36-am-scaled.webp
ORGANIZER;CN="Greenfield":MAILTO:greenfieldinfo@high.net
END:VEVENT
